:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03f01512-4546-59df-8e70-3aa004e3020a" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3 x\\right)\\cdot y=x^{4}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor.\n\nAssume $x>0$." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot y=x^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=3$ and $Q(x)=x^{3}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(3\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{3 x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223242e6-657c-5bec-8429-628abde472df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495317} {:answer/id #uuid "2616a25d-dc53-5253-a481-88bfdb77dd30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495319} {:answer/id #uuid "2824925e-5b26-5a3d-ac14-d9fecafbcf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495320} {:answer/id #uuid "91e8878f-4919-5880-ad79-fe8271c9a55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495345} {:answer/id #uuid "b97d76c6-b915-54b0-bcf7-c2824c4dd262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2824925e-5b26-5a3d-ac14-d9fecafbcf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495320} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d3a783d-5c90-57dd-b22c-25811200de97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fa0b599-1031-5002-a477-8a20611908f9" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-1$ and $Q(x)=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(-1\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a0cb4c-5470-5b60-b845-2fea9caa9516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495314} {:answer/id #uuid "732634a7-b684-5342-875a-b0080faf8912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495335} {:answer/id #uuid "91971313-09d0-59d7-a70f-11595c40eb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495344} {:answer/id #uuid "a06cec39-9592-52fd-a2e7-778b2eb94b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495349} {:answer/id #uuid "c88c1c16-6052-5ee3-ad30-dc668b434dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "732634a7-b684-5342-875a-b0080faf8912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495335} :answer-field/id #uuid "3060f3c4-885b-5427-ae2c-0db77cc62040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "979f5ce5-340c-5f1b-87a2-e39d8a750547" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x^{2}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=x^{2}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(1\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+y\\right) & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495382 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d91c400-f867-5cd9-a0e2-120b66efd8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495405} {:answer/id #uuid "59dec3ff-8460-51e7-a903-42017b8930fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495422} {:answer/id #uuid "c740fd19-86f8-5fe5-9930-6c80acd451a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495471} {:answer/id #uuid "cdea8f77-ad4b-5fc4-b32f-8bef94196c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c740fd19-86f8-5fe5-9930-6c80acd451a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495471} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ad4705b-ad41-530c-bbc3-049aeeb5f088" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495450} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3565d663-a155-53bb-ba0d-f96a68701312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{x} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495399} {:answer/id #uuid "7dbd634e-da6f-55e0-87f4-e0f9d870efd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495438} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c117eb-6f97-5654-b0e8-096b002a6949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495455} {:answer/id #uuid "a914a914-2dd2-5c22-a6ec-ab965d7d375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2 e^{x} - 1\\right) e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495456} {:answer/id #uuid "ded69673-685d-5972-b4d2-f1588dd9ce1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c117eb-6f97-5654-b0e8-096b002a6949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495455} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5859f24-99dc-5c7a-acd6-0bb431906896" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495489}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f2dc972-31dc-57c9-9e22-2efe43c996b3" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(1\\right)y=2,\\quad y(0)=3\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y) & =e^{x}\\cdot 2 \\\\ e^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+e^{x}y & =2 e^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x}) & =2 e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2 e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =2\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =2 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 2 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(2 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{2+C}{1} \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2 + e^{- x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25e71318-5920-5caf-9325-80e6065404cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 e^{x} - 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495393} {:answer/id #uuid "49202a76-3117-5bcc-aa4c-6349fef0d506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 12 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495413} {:answer/id #uuid "549dac5b-a505-5710-9807-2c1d539e1b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495418} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0660cc-710f-5461-ba04-d387305d719e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(6 e^{x} + 12\\right) e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495436} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ba0ee9-9174-572a-a7ec-3f4e29eb93d